# Paragraphs

Set paragraphs in body text: Arial regular, 19px, with a line height of 1.5. Use the variable `civica-font-size-body`, so the text grows with the font size scale.

## Supporting text

Use supporting text, 16px, for a short detail under a reading or a control, such as “Updated 14:05”. Use the variable `civica-font-size-small`. Use it sparingly. Most text on a card should be body text.

Do not go smaller than supporting text on a civica card. [Type scale](typography-type-scale.html#native-home-assistant-sizes) gives the smaller sizes that native Home Assistant screens keep.

<h2 id="bg-typ-02">Lay out text for reading</h2>

Left-align instructions, labels and help text, in English and in Welsh. A straight left edge makes long text quicker to read. Centre text only for a short, deliberate line, such as a large reading in the middle of a gauge.

Do not shorten a device name or an error message to fit the space. Let it wrap onto 2 lines. Do not cut it off with “…” if people need it to tell 2 devices apart.

This example shows a long device name on a card. Notice that the name and the Unavailable state wrap instead of being cut off.

